","typography_typography":"custom"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"d7eccaf","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p class="ds-markdown-paragraph">Getting stuck is embarrassing, but it happens to almost every Calgary driver at some point. Our winters are long, our spring thaws are messy, and our roads have soft shoulders that can swallow a tire in seconds. BP Towing doesn't judge – we just pull you out.</p><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Common stuck situations we handle:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in snow</strong> – A residential street after a blizzard, an unplowed alley, or your own driveway</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck on ice</strong> – Black ice on a side street or a frozen parking lot</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in mud</strong> – Spring or summer after heavy rain, on a rural road or job site</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in sand or gravel</strong> – Soft shoulders on country roads or construction areas</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in a ditch</strong> – You slid off the road on Deerfoot, Stoney, or a highway</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in a snowbank</strong> – You misjudged the edge of the plowed road</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in a field or off-road area</strong> – You took a wrong turn or went exploring</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stuck in a low-clearance situation</strong> – High-centred on a speed bump, curb, or rock</p></li></ul>","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"px","size":13,"sizes":[]},"paragraph_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":10,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"ddf6164","elType":"widget","settings":{"text":"Call Now | (403) 991-2265","link":{"url":"tel:+14039912265","is_external":"","nofollow":"","custom_attributes":""}