 <span>Vehicle Is Stuck?</span>","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":40,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.2,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"a2a7bc7","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p class="ds-markdown-paragraph">Before you call BP Towing, follow these steps to avoid making the situation worse:</p><ol start="1"><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stay calm</strong> – Panicking leads to bad decisions. You're stuck, but help is coming.</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stop spinning your wheels</strong> – Spinning digs you deeper. It melts snow into ice or creates ruts in mud. Stop now.</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Turn on hazard lights</strong> – Make yourself visible, especially at night or in poor weather.</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Assess your surroundings (if safe)</strong> – Are you on a busy road? In a ditch? In a parking lot? Note any obstacles (trees, rocks, signs).</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Call BP Towing</strong> – Tell us your exact location. Use Google Maps "what's my location" if you're unsure. Describe the stuck situation (snow, mud, ditch, etc.).</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Stay inside your vehicle</strong> – On busy roads or highways, do not exit. Wait inside with your seatbelt on. On quiet residential streets or rural areas, you may step out carefully – but stay visible.</p></li><li><p class="ds-markdown-paragraph"><strong>Do not accept help from strangers</strong> – A well-meaning driver with a tow strap can cause thousands of dollars in damage. Wait for our professional recovery team.</p></li></ol>","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_size_tablet":{"unit":"px","size":13,"sizes":[]},"paragraph_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":10,"sizes":[]}},"